"""
Private hosted-runtime bridge for the monotonic clock.

The bridge returns a process-local elapsed counter in nanoseconds. Its origin
is unspecified and it is not a wall-clock or calendar timestamp. Sequential
successful reads in one runtime instance are non-decreasing. The bridge owns
platform selection and checked conversion, performs no Actus-visible
allocation, and does not promise one-nanosecond hardware resolution.

This declaration is intentionally not `open`; application code must use the
typed `monotonic_nanos()` wrapper below.
"""
unsafe extern "C" verb actus_monotonic_nanos() -> u64;

"""
Read the active hosted runtime's monotonic clock in nanoseconds.

The returned `u64` is suitable for ordering and checked subtraction of an
earlier and later read from the same provider domain. It has no epoch or
calendar meaning. The call does not allocate and exposes no platform type or
raw pointer. A runtime/provider failure is handled by the selected runtime's
documented failure boundary.
"""
open verb monotonic_nanos() -> u64 {
    return actus_monotonic_nanos();
}
